# How line endings are handled in this repository.
#
# Without this file, the behaviour depends on each developer's local
# core.autocrlf setting, so the same file can look "entirely changed" to one
# person and unchanged to another. These rules live in the repository, so they
# apply identically on every machine and every clone.

# Treat everything as text unless it looks binary, and check it out with LF
# endings. LF is what .NET, Node and every CI runner expect, and it keeps the
# working tree byte-identical to what is stored.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---- Windows batch files genuinely require CRLF ----
# cmd.exe can misparse a .bat file that uses LF, so these are the exception.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# ---- Better diff headers ----
# Shows the enclosing method name in diff hunk headers instead of a bare line
# number, which makes reviewing a large C# change considerably easier.
*.cs text diff=csharp

# ---- Binary: never convert, never try to diff as text ----
# Line-ending conversion would corrupt these outright.
*.pdf binary
*.db  binary
*.db-shm binary
*.db-wal binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pfx binary
*.snk binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
